00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:15.930 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  blazblue persona 4 under night in birth  and Ruby for worlds that wonderfully  come together for a fast flashy and  endearing 2d tag fighter blaze blue  cross tag battle merges as an accessible  fighting game that breaks from the  series tradition by simplifying its  gameplay systems but by no means does  this make it shallow the dynamic tag  system and the clever ways you can mix  the game's unique mechanics our cross  tact shines here Arc System Works  unifies all franchises as a 5 button  fighter with two main attack buttons a  universal overhead attack that can also  function as an ax attack a tag button  and a partner skill while it may seem a  bit too straightforward even the most  historically complex characters on the  roster remain true to form where it  counts by distilling classic fighting  game mechanics the focus is shifted from  elaborate directional inputs to creating  openings for that suite high damage  combo especially once you factor in tag  assists and meter management you'll  recognize familiar moves with similar  properties from their respective games  but the conditions for execution have  changed basic attacks smart combos and  even super is called distortion skills  are easy to pull off  so the number of techniques mapped to  the limited controls can cause mistakes  particularly throws and distortion  skills auto forward - and most  characters may seem jarring to  fighting-game veterans but it doesn't  take that much effort to adjust to this  game's quirks and its pace partner  skills in particular will take time to  grasp every character has three unique  assist attacks where they fly in from  off-screen to lend a hand  cross combos take the tag system one  step further by letting your duo pylon  damage simultaneously  [Music]  these are the keys to executing great  combos creating openings or pulling  yourself out of a rut with this in mind  you're either encouraged to experiment  using different duo's or form your own  collaborative attacks with a pair that  you love most it's chaotic and sometimes  tough to nail down in live matches and  it's where the depth of the combat comes  from your effectiveness also revolves  around meter management the skill gauge  is used for distortion skills laying  down ax moves or saving up for  back-to-back supers with your tag  partner  the cross gage paves the way for cross  combos and tag counters and when you're  down a fighter the residents blaze kicks  you into overdrive by regenerating  health adding chip damage filling the  skill gauge and strengthening your  distortion skills  [Music]  Crosse tech battle has a lot to absorb  and it'll take time to get comfortable  with the fighting system and unravel all  of its intricacies thankfully the  onboarding process is top-notch tactics  mode walks you through the basic  terminology mechanics in their use cases  and each character has a tailor-made  tutorial that gives you the opportunity  to perfect specific combos and there's a  slew of missions in tactics mode that  pit you in difficult situations you'll  encounter in live matches all the pieces  of a fast smooth and endlessly fun  fighting game exists within cross tag  but it truly shines by channeling and  fusing the personality and charisma of  each franchise whether it's the stylish  super moves battle cries or fluid  animations this large cast is bursting  with charm  mixing up teams brings about  collaborations I've always wanted to see  happen  sure Ragna hide in Narukami may play  like the standard sword wielding boys  from their respective worlds but having  either them work together makes for a  badass team when I'm hopping from under  Knights Riverside stage one fight two  plays blues cathedral the next using my  favorite duo of Chie and Ruby while  listening to Hyde's battle theme cross  stack battle evokes and amplifies the  fondness I have for this roster and as a  diehard persona fan having the  investigation team reunited at Yasukuni  high for a hectic brawl while bumping  the arena mix to reach out to the truth  warms my heart especially smaller  moments like the unique chatter in  interactions between two characters  before fights commenced makes this feel  like more than a rehash of multiple  assets or a collection of characters  thrown together  [Music]  the crossing of worlds primarily plays  out in the episode mode the four  factions of Fighters are forced to  battle in a fake realm by a mysterious  omnipresent AI that creates arbitrary  rules yeah we are pleased to meet you  nice to meet you the overarching plot  sounds ridiculous and it's borderline  nonsensical each of the four campaigns  play out as a visual novel with static  character portraits and fully voiced  dialogue actual fights are embedded  within each chapter to keep you as an  active participant some character  appearances feel shoehorn for the sake  of making an appearance but despite its  absurdity moments of cross franchise  fanservice stick the landing  ruby's obsession with fancy weapons  permeates our encounters with the likes  of Ragna and hyde references the chi a's  obsession with steak and Yuki goes in  ability to make curry call back - when I  got to know them in persona 4 even Noel  gets caught up in the mix and she's  completely oblivious to how bad it'll  taste and as each episode concludes I  was rewarded with heartfelt scenes that  reminded me of why I love these  characters story mode also highlights  something odd DLC characters take part  in the story as opponents despite not  being available in the playable base  roster there movesets character models  theme songs and voice lines are in the  game but they're gated as add-on content  half of Ruby's cast is offered for free  but to see several persona BlazBlue and  under night folks  so obviously withheld feels unfair  [Music]  taking the fight online is where you'll  spend most of your time though cross  tags online component consists of  multiple lobbies for different skill  levels where players walk around as  chibi versions of their favorite  character customizing your player card  with character portraits and familiar  catchphrases is another avenue to  express your love it's cute and  light-hearted magnified by the adorable  batch of emotes that often take the edge  off exhilarating fights and thankfully  jumping into matches works seamlessly  after hundreds of rounds online both in  the casual Lobby and ranked matchmaking  we can say that the netcode is solid and  latency is a non-issue with a decent  connection players that want a more  competitive environment should be happy  to know that we have little trouble  finding a fair fight in ranked  matchmaking in both victory and defeat  memorable moments abound although it can  be frustrating I'm always taking note of  how high-level players are getting the  better of me  I'll also never forget making a comeback  from being down a teammate activating  resonance blaze and perfectly timing  both cheese power charge and godhand  while my opponent was a mid tag to take  them both out in one hit  [Music]  whether practicing in single-player or  competing against tough opponents online  cross tag battle is an absolute joy with  a surplus of possibilities within its  diverse roster and versatile fighting  system even with all the ridiculousness  of the overarching plot I reveled in the  charm of my favorite characters and  embrace the many moments of fanservice  it's a masterful unification of styles  and mechanics with four different  universes that compels you to dig deeper  and dedicate the time to getting the  most out of the beloved members of this  cast  [Music]

